WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.669
Speaker 1: We knew and we said it was going
to take a while to learn the full scope of

00:00:05.669 --> 00:00:12.270
the corruption and attempted coercion and
possible criminality of the last administration,

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:18.740
we knew we certainly didn't know everything
on January 20th when Donald Trump left office.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:24.380
And just about every week, certainly every
month, we have learned more and more in particular

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.989
about the efforts that the Trump administration
went to to try to steal the 2020 election

00:00:29.989 --> 00:00:32.950
in the period between November and January.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:40.200
There is a stunning, stunning new report from
The New York Times, where it is now known

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.550
that Donald Trump went to the Justice Department
and press them to declare the election results

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:48.550
corrupt.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:54.120
Trump wanted them to say this was a corrupt
election to then allow Trump to.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.260
We don't even know.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.360
That's the really scary part.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.870
Let's look at this important article.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.690
President Donald Trump pressed top Justice
Department officials late last year to declare

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.660
that the election was corrupt even though
they had found no instances of widespread

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.660
fraud.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:12.750
So he and his allies in Congress could use
the assertion to try to overturn the results.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:17.810
According to new documents provided to lawmakers,
the demands were an extraordinary instance

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:21.471
of a president interfering with an agency
that is typically more independent from the

00:01:21.471 --> 00:01:24.460
White House to advance his personal agenda.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:28.370
They are also the latest example of Trump's
wide ranging campaign during his final weeks

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:31.010
in office to delegitimize the election results.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.020
Remember William Barr said.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:41.310
In an interview, and certainly privately as
well, we found no evidence that fraud or improper

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.170
actions related to the election impacted the
results in any way, that that's what the DOJ

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.700
actually found.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:52.010
The article goes on to say that, listen to
this, the exchange unfolded during a phone

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:57.479
call on December 27th in which Trump pressed
the acting attorney general, Jeffrey Rosen,

00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:02.130
and his deputy, Richard Donahue, on voter
fraud claims that the Justice Department had

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:07.380
found no evidence for Mr. Donahue warned that
the department had no power to change the

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.599
outcome of the election.

00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:15.560
How many people told Trump that pense DOJ?
Trump replied, he did not expect that.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.260
According to notes Mr. Donohue took memorializing
the conversation.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:27.980
Just say the election was corrupt and leave
the rest to me and to congressional allies,

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.840
Donahue wrote in summarizing Trump's response.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:38.200
Trump was hoping that if the DOJ could just
say it was all corrupt, then Trump and his

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:43.650
Republican friends would figure out some way
to use that to, I guess, try to prevent Joe

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.350
Biden from actually taking office.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:50.140
Mr. Trump did not name the lawmakers, but
at other points during the call, he mentioned

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:55.280
Jim Jordan, Republican of Ohio, whom he described
as a fighter.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:02.930
Consider that Jim Jordan was named as one
of the five members of the House that Kevin

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:08.330
McCarthy wanted to put on this commission
to investigate what happened on January 6th.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:13.710
This is more evidence that Jim Jordan was
more of an accomplice than anything he could

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:18.879
be as an investigator has no business on that
committee.

00:03:18.879 --> 00:03:22.790
Representative Scott Perry, who at the time
promoted the idea that the election was stolen

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:27.450
from Trump, Senator Ron Johnson, who Trump
praised for getting to the bottom of things.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:32.370
Mr. Jordan and Mr. Johnson denied any role
in Trump's efforts to pressure the Justice

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.370
Department.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:37.780
Russell Dias, a spokesman for Jordan, remember,
Jordan voted to overturn the election results

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.670
in key states, quote, Congressman Jordan did
not and has not and would not pressure anyone

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:45.990
at the Justice Department about the 2020 election.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:50.620
Mr. Johnson had no conversations with President
Trump about the DOJ questioning the election

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.720
results, said his spokeswoman, Alexa Henning.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:58.409
She noted he had acknowledged Joseph Biden
as the president elect, but that he also called

00:03:58.409 --> 00:04:03.209
for what he sees as a rejection of an erection
election irregularities.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:07.820
That's my Chuck Schumer moment to be fully
investigated and addressed to restore confidence

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.340
in future elections.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.159
Perry did not respond to requests for comment.

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:15.599
He has continued to assert Trump won, but
has not been tied directly to the White House

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:17.430
to keep him in office.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:23.800
So, listen, I actually don't think there was
really a master plan here.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:30.740
I don't think Trump has the foresight or the
organization to really do this in an organized

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.020
manner.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:38.940
My sense is Trump had the idea he could coordinate
and put all of this stuff together.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.630
Let's let's get, you know, Rudy and other
people going around making claims and filing

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.350
court motions.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.449
Let's get the DOJ to say it was corrupt.

00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:50.590
Let's talk about getting people active.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:55.350
On January 6th. Trump might have had the idea
that he could put it all together is some

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.290
kind of master plan.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.330
I don't believe Trump is actually capable
of that.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:06.550
His general demeanor seems to have been, if
I can just get people, even if those people

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:11.100
don't really have the legal authority to change
anything related to the election, Rudy, going

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:18.000
around, get DOJ to say it was corrupt, get
Brad Raffensperger in Georgia to say we found

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.669
these, or maybe he could put it all together,
wrap it up and tie it with a bow and somehow

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:25.250
remain president.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:30.880
Now, he was probably closer to pulling it
off than we would like to admit.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:37.010
And what I mean by that is imagine if the
rioters, the terrorists, the insurrectionists

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:43.710
on January 6th had actually gotten to a Democratic
Congress member and held them hostage or gotten

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.250
to Mike Pence.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:50.730
They may have been successful in preventing
the certification of that election for a little

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:51.870
bit of time.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.449
Now, in a sense, they delayed it hours.

00:05:54.449 --> 00:05:57.250
They delayed it hours, but not days.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.960
Had they actually taken a hostage, which which
we believe many of them wanted to do, they

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:07.770
might have actually been able to delay it
further and consider how many times Trump

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:13.140
was told by different officials, you're being
told false information.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:16.250
None of the things you're saying are true.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:21.750
And Trump still would respond effectively
with I don't care, I don't care.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:27.740
Just say it's stolen and I'll figure out a
way to use it to try to keep the grift going.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:33.250
And then, of course, that also gets to what
a lot of this is about, which it's been.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:38.340
Used by Trump to continue raising money, but
that's the news, the sitting president pressured

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.410
the Department of Justice to say the election
was corrupt.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.590
That is an attempt to destroy our democracy.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:50.610
If he had gotten his way and if he had if
he had gotten someone at the DOJ to say that

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:54.990
and then he had used that to say the election
was corrupt, it's invalid.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:59.419
And I am going to, what, declare martial law
some kind of state of emergency, whatever.

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:03.479
He was ginning up with Mike Lendell, the my
pillow guy at the White House that day, that

00:07:03.479 --> 00:07:08.819
would have been a step towards the dictator
that Donald Trump very much wants to be.

00:07:08.819 --> 00:07:09.819
And think back.

00:07:09.819 --> 00:07:15.050
I mean, consider what we now know and then
think back to when Bill Clinton had a conversation

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.830
with Loretta Lynch.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.600
And that was like a big right wing scandal.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.340
You might not even remember that.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:24.830
And it seems laughable that that would even
count as a scandal, given what the former

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.260
administration tried to do.

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:28.949
It's absolutely crazy.

00:07:28.949 --> 00:07:33.410
And next, I want to talk about what's been
going on with the infrastructure bill, which

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.560
also sent Trump into a tizzy.

